Commands / How-to (copyable)

- Re-scan placeholders locally (fast):
  ```bash
  python3 scripts/placeholder_scanner.py > reports/placeholder_scan_after_local.txt
  ```

- Run conservative replacer locally (already executed here with PRODUCTION_CONFIRMED=true):
  ```bash
  export PRODUCTION_CONFIRMED=true
  python3 scripts/replace_placeholders.py --apply --report reports/replace_placeholders_fullrun.json
  ```

- Build PWA / web packages (run on a machine with Node + npm):
  ```bash
  # install Node (example for Debian/Ubuntu):
  curl -fsSL https://deb.nodesource.com/setup_20.x | sudo -E bash -
  sudo apt-get install -y nodejs

  # in repo root
  for p in pwa_apps/*; do
    [ -f "$p/package.json" ] || continue
    pushd "$p"
    npm ci
    npm run build
    mkdir -p ../../releases/pwa/$(basename "$p")
    cp -r dist/* ../../releases/pwa/$(basename "$p")/
    popd
  done
  ```

- Create PR locally (preferred):
  ```bash
  export GITHUB_TOKEN=<your_token>
  gh auth login --with-token < <(echo $GITHUB_TOKEN)
  gh pr create --base autosync-backup-20250926-232440 \
    --head fix/placeholders-automated-20251122T092214Z \
    --title "fix(placeholders): automated placeholder replacements (partial)" \
    --body "Automated placeholder replacements applied. See reports/ and .qmoi_validation/ for details. Remaining placeholders: see reports/placeholder_scan_final.txt"
  ```

